From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(render): animate native moving piston blocks

Create a Java moving piston block entity when translated native piston data arrives for the matching moving-piston state. Java 26.3 MovingPistonBlock.newBlockEntity returns null and ClientPacketListener.handleBlockEntityData only loads an existing entity, so remote translated piston updates previously disappeared without animation. Native server actor pushes remain authoritative; suppress Java local moving-piston entity pushes in Bedrock sessions to avoid duplication. Retain normal Java behavior outside Bedrock sessions.

Retain a distinct pending native moving-block entity until its separate
carried-block data arrives. Initialize direction from the translated block
state and keep empty geometry safe for chunk compilation and shape queries.
Do not advance Java's animation ticker while data is pending, since it
would eventually replace the native block with air. After loading, use
ordinary Java piston rendering and animation while suppressing duplicate
actor pushes as before. Ordinary Java piston instances keep their ticker.

The Enchanted protocol-2193 capture crashes in collision shape queries
through getMovementDirection before direction is initialized. A regression
reproduces the null-direction exception with the empty constructor. Another
integration test consumes the real core producer's NBT using Java 26.3's
codec, checking all directions and property-bearing carried blocks. The
previous Name/Properties representation silently decoded as air. These
checks establish Java lifecycle and codec behavior, not native parity.
